# The savefile corpus is binary and must never be line-ending converted.
#
# Git's own heuristic already gets this right -- `git ls-files --eol` reports
# every savefile as `i/-text`, because they carry NUL bytes early -- so this is
# belt and braces rather than a fix. It is here because the corpus is the one
# thing in the repository where a silent byte-for-byte change would go unnoticed
# until a character failed to load, and leaving that to a heuristic is a worse
# bargain than two lines of configuration.
#
# Written as individual attributes rather than the `binary` macro so the
# manifest below can opt back in: the macro is `-diff -merge -text` and a later
# `text` rule would re-enable conversion while leaving the file undiffable.
tests/saves/** -text -diff

# The manifest beside them is text, read a line at a time, and wants LF.
tests/saves/EXPECTED-FAILURES text eol=lf diff
